# CODEOWNERS — automatic reviewer requests, routed by what a pull request touches.
#
# Two teams, mirroring the roles in GOVERNANCE.md §3 and CORE-TEAM.md:
#
#   @croa-project/core-team   — writes the framework; holds write authority over
#                               the specification. Owns normative surfaces.
#   @croa-project/maintainers — core team members carrying the operational load:
#                               triage, releases, RFC process, final call on
#                               merges. Owns project-level commitments and CI.
#
# ⚠️ Both teams must EXIST in the croa-project organization for these rules to
#    fire. GitHub requests nobody, silently, for a team that does not exist.
#    Until the teams are created, replace the handles below with individuals:
#      core-team   → @Yaouldha @darrinps @sdurand06
#      maintainers → @Yaouldha @darrinps
#
# Later rules win: the most specific match applies.

# Default: the people who write the framework.
*                       @croa-project/core-team

# ── Normative surfaces ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The specification and everything an implementer relies on to claim conformance.
/spec/                  @croa-project/core-team
/rfcs/                  @croa-project/core-team
/public-review/         @croa-project/core-team

# ── Project-level commitments ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changing these changes what the project promises, not what it specifies.
/GOVERNANCE.md          @croa-project/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md     @croa-project/maintainers
/SECURITY.md            @croa-project/maintainers
/CITATION.cff           @croa-project/maintainers
/LICENSE                @croa-project/maintainers
/LICENSE-CODE           @croa-project/maintainers
/LICENSE-DOCS           @croa-project/maintainers
/CORE-TEAM.md           @croa-project/maintainers
/MAINTAINERS.md         @croa-project/maintainers

# ── The guardrails themselves ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Whoever can change these can remove the rest. Maintainers own them.
/.github/               @croa-project/maintainers

# ── Evidence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports from implementers, including failures. Reviewed by the core team,
# which acts on them (CORE-TEAM.md, "How the core team works with implementers").
/evidence/              @croa-project/core-team
